# <%= current_page.data.title %>

Beyond the [application charts](application-charts.html), [cpp-helm-chart](https://github.com/hmcts/cpp-helm-chart/tree/main) holds the charts that build and support the platform itself. These are operated by the platform teams — service teams rarely change them, but you will see their releases in every cluster and their names in `cpp-aks-deploy` and `cpp-flux-config`, so it helps to know what each one is.

Many wrap a well-known upstream chart (istio, kube-prometheus-stack, Velero and so on), pinned and configured for CPP; the rest are CPP-specific. Each links to its directory in the repository, which is the authoritative reference for its values.

## Cluster infrastructure

| Chart | Purpose |
|---|---|
| [istio-base](https://github.com/hmcts/cpp-helm-chart/tree/main/istio-base), [istiod](https://github.com/hmcts/cpp-helm-chart/tree/main/istiod), [istio-ingress](https://github.com/hmcts/cpp-helm-chart/tree/main/istio-ingress), [istio-egress](https://github.com/hmcts/cpp-helm-chart/tree/main/istio-egress) | The [istio](https://istio.io) service mesh: cluster resources and CRDs, the control plane, and the ingress/egress gateways |
| [istio-config](https://github.com/hmcts/cpp-helm-chart/tree/main/istio-config) | istio configuration for an application or context namespace |
| [istio-authorization-policies](https://github.com/hmcts/cpp-helm-chart/tree/main/istio-authorization-policies) | AuthorizationPolicy resources controlling which workloads may talk to which |
| [flux-operator](https://github.com/hmcts/cpp-helm-chart/tree/main/flux-operator), [flux-instance](https://github.com/hmcts/cpp-helm-chart/tree/main/flux-instance) | The [Flux](https://fluxcd.io) operator and the Flux instance it manages — the foundation of the GitOps route |
| [keda](https://github.com/hmcts/cpp-helm-chart/tree/main/keda) | [KEDA](https://keda.sh) event-driven autoscaling |
| [gatekeeper](https://github.com/hmcts/cpp-helm-chart/tree/main/gatekeeper) | OPA Gatekeeper policy enforcement |
| [azure-service-operator](https://github.com/hmcts/cpp-helm-chart/tree/main/azure-service-operator) | [Azure Service Operator](https://github.com/Azure/azure-service-operator), which lets charts declare Azure resources (for example federated identity credentials) as Kubernetes objects |
| [aks-rbac](https://github.com/hmcts/cpp-helm-chart/tree/main/aks-rbac) | Cluster-level RBAC for AKS |
| [ccm-namespace](https://github.com/hmcts/cpp-helm-chart/tree/main/ccm-namespace) | Creates and configures CCM namespaces |
| [cpp-platform-priming](https://github.com/hmcts/cpp-helm-chart/tree/main/cpp-platform-priming) | Primes a cluster with CPP platform prerequisites |
| [overprovisioning](https://github.com/hmcts/cpp-helm-chart/tree/main/overprovisioning) | Headroom pods that keep spare capacity available for fast scale-up |
| [dynatrace-operator](https://github.com/hmcts/cpp-helm-chart/tree/main/dynatrace-operator) | Dynatrace observability agent operator |
| [kiali-operator](https://github.com/hmcts/cpp-helm-chart/tree/main/kiali-operator) | Kiali service-mesh observability for istio |
| [velero](https://github.com/hmcts/cpp-helm-chart/tree/main/velero) | [Velero](https://velero.io) cluster backup and restore |

## Monitoring and dashboards

| Chart | Purpose |
|---|---|
| [kube-prometheus-stack](https://github.com/hmcts/cpp-helm-chart/tree/main/kube-prometheus-stack), [kube-prometheus-stack-v3](https://github.com/hmcts/cpp-helm-chart/tree/main/kube-prometheus-stack-v3) | Prometheus Operator, Prometheus rules and Grafana dashboards for cluster monitoring |
| [prometheus-adapter](https://github.com/hmcts/cpp-helm-chart/tree/main/prometheus-adapter), [prometheus-adapter-v3](https://github.com/hmcts/cpp-helm-chart/tree/main/prometheus-adapter-v3) | Exposes Prometheus metrics through the Kubernetes metrics APIs, so autoscalers can use them |
| [prometheus-node-exporter](https://github.com/hmcts/cpp-helm-chart/tree/main/prometheus-node-exporter) | Node-level metrics |
| [kube-state-metrics](https://github.com/hmcts/cpp-helm-chart/tree/main/kube-state-metrics) | Cluster-object metrics |
| [grafana](https://github.com/hmcts/cpp-helm-chart/tree/main/grafana) | Grafana on its own, where the full stack is not wanted |
| [filebeat](https://github.com/hmcts/cpp-helm-chart/tree/main/filebeat) | Ships container logs to Elasticsearch |
| [smashing](https://github.com/hmcts/cpp-helm-chart/tree/main/smashing) | Smashing status dashboards |

Where a `-v3` variant exists it is maintained in parallel with the original — check which of the two your target cluster consumes in `cpp-aks-deploy` or `cpp-flux-config` before changing either.

